
# RoomSell AI Engineering Rules

## Product principles
- Accurate geometry is more important than attractive AI output.
- A locked object must never change automatically.
- Retailer product IDs, prices and dimensions are authoritative.
- Never invent SKUs, inventory or quotations.
- No feature is complete without acceptance tests.

## Architecture
- Use TypeScript.
- Keep scene-core and layout-engine framework-independent.
- Persist positions in metres.
- Use versioned scene operations.
- Treat the backend as authoritative for committed edits.
- Keep retailer data isolated by organisation.
- Validate all external inputs.

## AI restrictions
- AI may propose layout intentions.
- AI cannot bypass geometry validation.
- AI cannot change locks directly.
- AI cannot invent catalogue data or prices.
- AI output must be schema-validated.

## Coding workflow
- Work on one issue or bounded milestone at a time.
- Add tests for every geometry rule.
- Run lint, typecheck and tests before completing a task.
- Do not silently modify unrelated modules.
- Document migrations and architectural changes.
- Do not hardcode credentials or secrets.
- Never claim success without verification.

## Definition of done
- Feature works in a running application.
- Tests cover expected behaviour and failure modes.
- No critical security or data-integrity regressions.
- Relevant documentation is updated.
- Code has been reviewed.
